 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "Offline adaptation of the interactive task: n nodes and the hidden set badNodes are given, and test(list) is simulated as \"no listed node is bad\". The searcher uses a fixed divide-and-conquer strategy: test the whole range [0, n); whenever a tested range [lo, hi) fails and holds more than one node, test [lo, mid) and then [mid, hi) with mid = floor((lo + hi) / 2); a failing single node is bad. Return [the bad nodes in ascending order, the number of test calls made].",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-b-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
